{
  "$comment": [
    "The third-party inventory THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is generated from. Edited by hand;",
    "`scripts/gen-notices.mjs` renders it and, when the macOS library set is present, refuses",
    "to render if any shipped dylib has no entry here. That check is the whole point of the",
    "`libs` field — a dependency added to the build lands in the notices or fails the gate.",
    "",
    "`license` is the license of THE ARTIFACT WE SHIP, which is not always the project's",
    "headline license. FFmpeg and mpv are the cases that matter: Homebrew's own formulae are",
    "GPL-3.0 and GPL-2.0, and copying those here would mislabel our own non-GPL builds as GPL.",
    "Where a project is multi-licensed, `license` records the option taken and `note` says so.",
    "",
    "`libs` lists the file stems shipped for that project (no version, no extension). An empty",
    "list means the project ships no file of its own: it is statically inside the prebuilt",
    "Windows libmpv-2.dll. Those entries cannot be verified against a closure, so they are",
    "over-inclusive by design — listing a component the current upstream build happens not to",
    "carry costs nothing, while omitting one that it does carry is the actual violation."
  ],
  "projects": [
    {
      "id": "mpv",
      "name": "mpv",
      "license": "LGPL-2.1-or-later",
      "text": "mpv",
      "url": "https://mpv.io/",
      "source": "https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv",
      "libs": ["libmpv", "libmpv-2"],
      "note": "Built with -Dgpl=false, which is what makes it LGPL rather than GPL-2.0-or-later. On macOS by scripts/build-macos-libs.sh; on Windows this is upstream's own LGPL build, whose embedded configuration string records the same flag."
    },
